-- title:
--   Order of a Hopf algebra splits along its Frobenius kernel
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be a field of characteristic $p$, for a prime $p$, and let $H$ be a commutative ring carrying a Hopf algebra structure over $k$, finite-dimensional as a $k$-module and cocommutative as a $k$-coalgebra. Write $I = \ker(\varepsilon)$ for the kernel of the counit algebra map $H \to k$, and let $J = \langle a^p : a \in I\rangle$ be the ideal of $H$ generated by the $p$-th powers of the elements of $I$. On the Cartier dual $\mathrm{CartierDual}\ k\ H$, which by definition is the $k$-linear dual $\mathrm{Hom}_k(H,k)$ equipped with its ring structure as a commutative ring and Hopf algebra over $k$, let $\mathfrak{b}$ be the ideal generated by the set of those functionals $\varphi$ with $\varphi(1) = 0$ and $\varphi(x) = 0$ for every $x \in J$. The assertion is the multiplicative identity of $k$-dimensions $$\dim_k\bigl(H/J\bigr)\cdot \dim_k\bigl(\mathrm{CartierDual}\ k\ H/\mathfrak{b}\bigr) = \dim_k H.$$
--
--   In the language of finite commutative group schemes $G = \operatorname{Spec} H$ over $k$, this is the multiplicativity of orders along the Frobenius kernel, $|G| = |G[F]| \cdot |G/G[F]|$, combined with the invariance of order under Cartier duality: $H/J$ is the coordinate ring of $G[F]$, while the quotient of the Cartier dual by $\mathfrak{b}$ is the coordinate ring of the kernel of the restriction map $G^\vee \to G[F]^\vee$. It serves the dimension bookkeeping for formal groups and $p$-divisible groups, being used in the computation of heights and cotangent dimensions under Cartier duality.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_HopfAlgebra_finrank_quotient_span_pow_mul_finrank_cartierDual_quotient_eq.lean

